      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-48707",
      ":question/problem": "Susan, the new receptionist of the Smithsonian Museum in Washington DC, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of visitors to the museum $t$ minutes after the museum has opened.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the museum\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the museum\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the museum\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?"
