      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-72004",
      ":question/problem": "Jason, a biologist, is measuring the growth of bacteria in a Petri dish by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of bacteria in the dish.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of bacteria in the dish is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $N(t)$ and $r(t)?$"
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186233149,
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-112509",
      ":question/problem": "Joseph is measuring the height reached by his lime tree by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in years, since he planted the tree:\n\n- $H(t)$ - The tree's height, in centimeters\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the tree's height is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $H(t)$ and $r(t)?$"
    },
